            <ArticleTitle>[A man with upper abdominal pain and a pancytopenia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A8502</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 41-year-old man visited his general practitioner because of upper abdominal pain. Physical examination revealed splenomegaly. Laboratory testing showed pancytopenia with a striking monocytopenia with hairy cells. Immunological and molecular analysis confirmed the diagnosis hairy cell leukemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
